  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Environment Programme: Core Contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia is a Member State of the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP), which leads the implementation of the environmental dimension of sustainable development in the UN system. UNEP assists developing countries in implementing multilateral environment agreements and environmentally sound policies and practices, including relating to the atmosphere, marine and terrestrial ecosystems, environmental governance, chemicals, waste and green economy. The Department of Climate Change, Energy, the Environment and Water provides an annual contribution to UNEP&apos;s Environment Fund.</narrative>
  </description>
